WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.564
Building a wireless

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.684
network adapter for

00:00:02.496 --> 00:00:03.734
the Super Nintendo

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.468
A hobbyist built

00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:06.636
a wireless network

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:07.426
adapter for the

00:00:07.237 --> 00:00:08.345
Super Nintendo

00:00:08.523 --> 00:00:09.937
bringing the 1990s

00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:11.235
console online with

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:12.237
homebrew hardware

00:00:12.766 --> 00:00:13.968
In practice this

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.735
makes the save

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.126
sync delay imperceptible

00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:17.152
and only when

00:00:16.964 --> 00:00:18.049
an existing save

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.685
is pulled by

00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:19.570
the SNES for

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:20.372
the first time

00:00:20.266 --> 00:00:20.832
is there a

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:22.659
1-2s load screen

00:00:23.198 --> 00:00:24.223
The challenge was

00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:24.742
the time to

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:25.414
first token of

00:00:25.226 --> 00:00:26.098
the LLM

00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:27.018
for Haiku it

00:00:26.842 --> 00:00:28.280
was about 0.8

00:00:28.104 --> 00:00:28.587
s

00:00:28.764 --> 00:00:29.624
but for Opus

00:00:29.436 --> 00:00:30.945
it averaged 2.2

00:00:30.757 --> 00:00:31.381
s

00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:32.916
Full story on

00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:33.623
the dashboard
